From 089bcdb118b56383bd4f79ce53bb1392b5db23a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiasClear <noreply@biasclear.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:02:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Explain drafts: settings stop within 15 minutes;
 network-address handling disclosed (306)

Draft wording only; the public site is unchanged.

- Consent said "Explain pauses if that setting changes", but each warm
  instance rechecks the account settings every 15 minutes
  (SETTINGS_INTERVAL_MS), so traffic can continue that long. It now says
  "stops within 15 minutes", in the generator, SITE_CONTRACT and SPEC.
- The drafts never said the service reads the visitor's network address.
  Consent now says it keeps only a code made from it; the privacy draft
  says how (salted hash with a daily random key, only as a request count,
  about an hour or to the end of the next day), that the address is never
  stored or logged, that each key expires after two days and Amazon
  erases expired items within a few days, and that AWS handles the
  connection.
- PRIVACY-DRAFTS.md regenerated (--check passes).

Regression: test/privacy.test.ts holds the copy to SETTINGS_INTERVAL_MS
and SALT_TTL_MS and requires the address wording for every model; it
fails on the old generator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
